/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Superficial pigment refers to pigmentation that has formed on the superficial layer of the skin, including acne scars, spots, inflammatory pigmentation, etc. The coverage of pigmentation may exist in both deep and shallow layers. You can compare the image with the deep pigment image. If the shallow layer shows pigmentation but the deep layer shows no pigmentation, it means that the pigment is only deposited in the superficial layer of the skin, The algorithm marks the pigmented area with a purple polygon curve, and the shallow pigment can be seen more clearly and intuitively through the form of data.)
/Pg 10 0 R
